=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED
issue: 471
title: an assertion that reads the fixture's value through the test's own assignment takes the producer's evidence
origin: ruling 471 Q3 (b): `result = provider.resolve_voice("")`, then `assert result == ...`, reads the
origin2: fixture `provider` through the unit's own assignment (frontend _resolve_through), so the finding
origin3: takes the evidence of Provider(), the call the conftest fixture returns. The test calls only
origin4: resolve_voice through the fixture's value, which matches no changed symbol from its imports.
=== before: voices.py ===
class Provider:
    def resolve_voice(self, name):
        return name.lower() if name else "rachel"
=== after: voices.py ===
class Provider:
    def resolve_voice(self, name):
        return name.lower() if name else "matilda"
=== before: tests/test_voices.py ===
def test_resolve_default(provider):
    result = provider.resolve_voice("")
    assert result == "rachel"
=== after: tests/test_voices.py ===
def test_resolve_default(provider):
    result = provider.resolve_voice("")
    assert result == "matilda"
=== head: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest

from voices import Provider


@pytest.fixture
def provider():
    return Provider()
